# WLW sync-tool pair (hard rule)

Two tools must stay **behaviourally matched** for the WLW app-tree mirror. Both live under **wanos** and share **`helpers/wanos-sync.config.txt`**:

| Side | Repo | Tool |
|---|---|---|
| PC → Pi live | **wanos** | `helpers/wanos-sync.ps1` (`… wlw`) — `[MirrorExclude*]` from config |
| Pi clone → Pi live | **wanos** | `helpers/wlw-sync.sh` — same config sections (deploy via main WanOS sync) |

be90webserver has **no** `helpers/wlw-sync.sh` — do not re-add one. Pi operators run `bash ~/wanos/helpers/wlw-sync.sh`.

Product locks: be90webserver `docs/wlw-sync.md`. This repo: [`docs/wanos-sync.md`](docs/wanos-sync.md) (WLW pair section).

## Locked match (both tools)

| Topic | Lock |
|---|---|
| Compare | `--checksum --no-times` (not size+mtime). PC: `-ContentChecksum` on the wlw mirror job only; main/LCD stay `-avz`. |
| Excludes SSoT | `helpers/wanos-sync.config.txt` `[MirrorExcludeDirs]` / `[MirrorExcludeFiles]` — **one list** for main + lcd + wlw + Pi sh |
| Dir excludes (locked set) | `.git`, `.cursor`, `.idea`, `.venv`, `docs`, `code-import`, `backup*`, `logs`, `temp`, `wanos_venv`, `migration_venv`, `billit_venv`, `__pycache__`, `sessionlog`, **`_archive`** — **not** bare `bootstrap`, **not** `_lcd-agent`, **not** `aistudio-preview` |
| File excludes (high level) | `.env*`, `*.md`, gitignore/attrs, sync `.bat`/`.ps1`, Pi-owned WanOS YAML/db, `ssh-term-full.js`, WLW symlinks `db+credentials`/`logs`, `*.lnk`, `_tmp*`, `*.pyc`, … — **not** `LICENSE`; **no** AI Studio `server.ts`/`tsconfig.json`/`metadata.json`/`package.json` |
| LF normalize (PC) | Deploy text set incl. **`.svg`**, **`.sudoers`**, **`.timer`**; be90 `.gitattributes` `eol=lf` for the same types |
| Sync vs gitignore | Sync does **not** read `.gitignore`; `_archive` exclude covers gitignored archive dirs |

## When either side changes

If you change **any** of: mirror excludes, compare rules, modes, path locks, or the WLW LF-normalize extension set — in the **same** authorized code turn:

1. Update **config** (`wanos-sync.config.txt`) and ensure PC + Pi tools both read it (no hardcoded EXCLUDE_* drift).
2. Update **both** product docs (`docs/wanos-sync.md` here · be90webserver `docs/wlw-sync.md`).
3. Update **both** `.cursor/rules/wlw-sync-pair.mdc` copies when the locked match table changes.
4. Do **not** leave one tool ahead of the other.

## Do not

- Add WLW mirror excludes only in a script array (use config)
- Reuse bare path segment `bootstrap` (would skip be90 `helpers/bootstrap/`)
- Re-add AI Studio exclude names (`aistudio-preview`, `server.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `metadata.json`, `package.json`)
- Drop `--checksum` / `--no-times` on only one side of the WLW pair
